{# TM·K — the counts, and they sit at the TOP of the page. Standing rule, no
   exceptions; the preset's key order puts them there, so nothing here enforces
   it and nothing here can break it either.

   EVERY NUMBER IS A QUERY over team_user and team_position at render time,
   never a stored counter — a person who is deactivated stops being counted as
   active because the column says so.

   A FRESH INSTALLATION GETS NO STRIP AT ALL. Four of the five counts would be
   zero, and a strip of zeros is a strip that says nothing. The honest first-run
   fact is a sentence, and the useful thing to do from it is a button. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiTeam/team/_bits.html.twig' as bits %}

{% if overview.isFirstRun %}
    <div class="tm-fresh">
        {{ bits.icon_people(1.6) }}
        <div class="ft">
            <b>You are the only person here.</b>
            <p>A fresh installation has one account &mdash; the Super Admin the installer created &mdash; and no
            positions. Everyone you add lands as <b>Staff with no position</b>, which means they can sign in and
            do nothing at all, so the first useful thing to make is a position for them to hold.</p>
            <div class="fdo">
                <a class="cta" href="{{ path('team_positions') }}">{{ bits.icon_plus() }} Make the first position</a>
                <a class="softbtn" href="{{ path('team_invite') }}">Add a person first</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
{% else %}
    <div class="grid w-flush dp-kstrip">
        <div class="c kpi">
            <span class="tab">People</span>
            <b class="disp">{{ overview.people }}</b>
            <span class="sub">{{ overview.active }} active{% if overview.deactivated %} &middot; <span class="fog">{{ overview.deactivated }} deactivated</span>{% endif %}</span>
        </div>

        {# No link to the matrix on this sub-line. It was the longest thing on the
           strip and the only one that wrapped, and it was the THIRD route to the
           same page: the header carries "Positions & permissions" and every
           position name in the table below is a link to it. A KPI sub-line says
           what the number is made of; it is not navigation. #}
        <div class="c kpi">
            <span class="tab">Positions</span>
            <b class="disp">{{ overview.positions }}</b>
            <span class="sub">{{ overview.departments }} department{{ overview.departments == 1 ? '' : 's' }} &middot; {{ overview.positionsHeld }} of {{ overview.positions }} held</span>
        </div>

        <div class="c kpi">
            <span class="tab">Never signed in</span>
            <b class="disp">{{ overview.neverSignedIn|length }}</b>
            <span class="sub">
                {%- if overview.neverSignedIn is empty -%}<span class="fog">everybody has arrived</span>
                {%- else -%}
                    {%- for person in overview.neverSignedIn|slice(0, 2) -%}
                        {{ loop.first ? '' : ' &middot; ' }}<span class="w">{{ person.firstName|slice(0, 1) }}. {{ person.lastName }}</span>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                    {%- if overview.neverSignedIn|length > 2 %} &middot; <span class="fog">and {{ overview.neverSignedIn|length - 2 }} more</span>{% endif -%}
                {%- endif -%}
            </span>
        </div>

        <div class="c kpi">
            <span class="tab">Hold nothing</span>
            <b class="disp">{{ overview.holdNothing|length }}</b>
            <span class="sub">
                {%- if overview.holdNothing is empty -%}<span class="fog">everybody holds a position</span>
                {%- else -%}
                    {%- for person in overview.holdNothing|slice(0, 2) -%}
                        {{ loop.first ? '' : ' &middot; ' }}<span class="w">{{ person.firstName|slice(0, 1) }}. {{ person.lastName }}</span>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                    &middot; no position
                {%- endif -%}
            </span>
        </div>

        {# THE COUNT THE TIER COLUMN NO LONGER ANSWERS. Some of these people are
           administrators because of their tier and some because a position they
           hold carries team.manage. One number, two mechanisms, and the sub-line
           has to name both or the number is unreadable. #}
        <div class="c kpi hot">
            <span class="tab">Can administer</span>
            <b class="disp">{{ overview.administrators }}<em>of {{ overview.people }}</em></b>
            <span class="sub">{{ overview.administratorsByTier }} by tier &middot; {{ overview.administratorsByPermission }} by <span class="mono">team.manage</span></span>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endif %}
